CSP illustrates the cost of conditioning on reference success. Its primary ratio was 1.073. On the full test split the schedule solved 12 additional instances and its fixed-slot ratio was 0.972. A similar, smaller change of sign occurred on SAT. Both the choice of population and the timeout charge therefore matter to the performance claim.

= Interpretation and limits
For a new benchmark, saving one extra scalar, the total backup time on routed instances, identifies the aggregate runtime ratio under the stated additive model. Saving the flags as well permits different workload mixes and subgroup analyses. The query problem is relevant when older or separately maintained records preserve only the count and a few pairings can be reconstructed. If individual checks require replaying a randomized policy, the original flag must be recoverable from its seed or trace. Without that information the check can measure a different decision.

The audit addresses a fixed archive. The logs used here supply the complete pairing; we mask it to study what can be established after partial release. Our experiments give no estimate of the frequency of missing joins in the literature. The first-stage attempts are time-limited portfolio members. A learned front end would also require evidence about the quality of its accepted answers. Process start-up, transfers and supervision can add time to a live portfolio. As a sensitivity to fixed overhead, a schedule with observed $R<1$ can absorb at most $B(1-R)/n$ additional seconds per evaluated instance before losing its advantage. For ASP on the primary panel this is about 1.63 seconds. The finite-panel calculations alone cannot predict performance on another machine or workload.

For statistical sampling, randomized designs can target mean squared error and design-unbiasedness under bounded outcomes [7]. Our deterministic intervals instead guarantee both endpoints for every admissible labeling on the recorded instances. Under a model for dependence, a targeted decision loss or a randomization-based coverage criterion, different checks may be preferable. DeepOPF+ gives a concrete reporting example [8]. Its Table II includes conditional projection time in the reported mean and distinguishes its mean instance-wise speedup from the ratio of mean times. Once a compatible end-to-end total is released, the aggregate comparison is directly available. Extending this guarantee to multiple backups with route-specific costs would require optimizing over assignments of several label types. The binary majority argument uses the exact count of a single route.

= Conclusion
A fallback rate and a distribution of reference times can support a wide range of aggregate runtimes. For an exact count and uniformly priced checks, the narrowest guaranteed interval is computable by sorting and scanning. Separate known counts support optimal allocation across panels. The empirical returns to checking the slowest runs were substantial on these six archives, yet a small time difference could remain unresolved even after checking half of the flags. Reporting the sum of backup times on routed instances would remove this ambiguity at its source.

*Data and code.* The ASlib repository supplies the benchmark logs. The replication package pins their revision and hashes and includes the replay, independent reconstruction, enumeration tests and manuscript data. #link("https://github.com/coseal/aslib_data")[ASlib data] · #link("https://github.com/fightforbelief/p3-solver-speed-audit")[Replication package].

